Language: en

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:04.950 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  there was no doubt who they'd come to  see a monarch like no other marking a  moment that britain has never seen  before  had camped out overnight to get a front  row seat for the start of the platinum  jubilee  as the military began their procession  the police were forced to respond  the crowds turning against the animal  rights protesters tried to delay  proceedings  normal service resumed it was time for  the main event the queen's birthday  parade formal and official but at the  heart a family occasion  clear from the very first carriage as  prince george princess charlotte and  prince louis took their first ride down  the mall  their father prince william joined  prince charles and princess anne on  horseback  with the queen unable to travel to watch  the irish guards troop their colour the  trio dispatched to deputize on her  behalf  from the windows of the major general's  office the younger royals watched and  maybe learned  and caught up with those they haven't  seen in a while  it wasn't a secret we knew that megan  and harry were going to be there but  they kept a low profile for the cameras  at buckingham palace the symbol went up  the queen had returned  and then she appeared with her cousin  the duke of kent  in a first for her and for the military  taking the salute from the palace  balcony and casting an expert eye on the  display  as the military returned to barracks and  the crowds were ushered forward you  could see the numbers that had come out  a much needed celebration for many even  during these difficult times and  reaffirmed by this reaction  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  as the queen stepped out with her heirs  and working royals around her  the flypast always a family favorite  prince louis looking less certain at  times  reassured by his great-grandmother  other members of the family not sticking  to the script included prince charles  and camilla walking back to clarence  house  a chance to thank the crowds how was it  you royal highness how was it  quite warm  in another unexpected twist we've now  been told that prince andrew has got  covet we weren't actually expecting to  see him on horse guards for trooping the  color but there are other events  throughout this jubilee where he could  have put in an appearance especially  when the queen has already shown us very  clearly that this is a weekend when she  wants her relatives around her  there was one final duty of the day that  she didn't want to delegate pressing the  button in windsor that would eventually  light up the principal beacon in london  [Music]  [Applause]  overseen by prince william  [Music]  tomorrow her family will again have to  represent her the queen no longer  attending the thanksgiving service at  saint paul's we're told that she has  enjoyed today immensely tomorrow she  needs rest  rhiannon mills sky news at buckingham  palace

